```

<!-- stacks:fill The two or three calls people make most, with one line each on what they do. -->

The Javadoc (`make docs`, or the `-javadoc.jar` on Maven Central) documents every public type with examples. [docs/public-api.md](docs/public-api.md) lists the exports and what counts as a breaking change.

## Development

Requires the JDK named in `.java-version` (on macOS, `brew install openjdk@<major>`; the Makefile finds it) and make. Maven comes from the committed wrapper, `./mvnw`.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make test` | Unit, property and example tests |
| `make docs` | Javadoc, failing on any doclint warning |
| `make build` | The jar, sources jar and Javadoc jar under `target/` |
| `make test-consumer` | Builds a separate project against the installed jar |
| `make api-check` | Fails on an incompatible change since the last release |
| `make ci` | Everything CI runs |

Releasing is a person's step: [docs/releasing.md](docs/releasing.md).

